.TH MOGUET 1 "September 2026" "Moguet @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.\" parity:name
.SH NAME
moguet \- pacman-first AUR helper with verified source builds
.
.\" parity:synopsis
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moguet
.I operation
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ targets... ]
.
.B moguet
.B -S --select [--needed]
.I query
.
.B moguet
.B -Syu [--needed]
.
.B moguet
.B -Syu --repo [--needed]
.
.B moguet
.BR -h | --help
.
.B moguet
.BR -V | --version
.
.B moguet
.B --dry-run
.I supported-operation
.
.\" parity:description
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Moguet
is a pacman-first AUR helper for Arch Linux with verified source builds and
per-package build preferences.
It keeps package transactions with
.BR pacman (8),
package builds with
.BR makepkg (8),
and repository transport with
.BR git (1).
Moguet owns planning, review, artifact validation, and the safe hand-off
between those tools.
.
.PP
Run
.B moguet
as a normal user.
It invokes
.B sudo pacman
only for operations that require a system package transaction.
AUR source retrieval, review, and builds are not run as root.
Moguet is not an official Arch Linux, pacman, or AUR project, an independent
package manager, or a complete clone of another AUR helper.
.
.PP
The name combines the Japanese expression \(dqもぐもぐ\(dq and the English
diminutive suffix
.IR -let ,
then shapes the resulting Mogulet toward lowercase French
.IR muguet ,
meaning lily of the valley.
The flower is small and modest but poisonous, reflecting a helper that warns
about danger or ambiguity and stops before unprovable mutation.
The formal project name and reading are \(dqMoguet\(dq and \(dqモグエット\(dq.
.
.PP
Operations handled entirely by pacman preserve compatible pacman arguments
that Moguet does not consume.
When a target enters an AUR or source-build route, an option whose meaning
cannot be preserved is rejected before external mutation instead of being
silently ignored.
Exact target-less
.B -Syu
is an intercepted ordinary AUR-helper update: it completes the official
repository system upgrade and then performs a fresh normal installed-AUR
update without reading saved source-build preferences.
The explicit
.BR upgrade ,
.BR upgrade-aur ,
and
.B upgrade-all
commands are source-aware workflows that check and apply saved preferences.
Command and option tokens are locale-independent.
Closed Moguet grammar accepts only environment assignments after the one
primary remote or local build operand. It rejects an extra bare build operand,
and rejects target operands for
.BR upgrade ,
.BR upgrade-aur ,
.BR upgrade-all ,
.BR clean ,
and
.BR list-src .
.BR deps ,
.BR plan ,
.BR fetch ,
and source-maintenance forms marked with an ellipsis remain multi-target.
.
.\" parity:commands
.SH COMMANDS
.\" PUBLIC COMMANDS BEGIN
.TP
.B "build <pkg> [V=K...] | build --local <directory> [V=K...]"
Without
.BR --local ,
build one official-repository or AUR package from source without saving a
source-build preference.
With
.BR --local ,
treat exactly one user-owned directory as a local PackageBase source and never
infer that source from a path-like package operand.
A safe existing
.I .SRCINFO
is read without modification. Missing, invalid, or known-stale metadata is
evaluated through
.B makepkg --printsrcinfo
only after PKGBUILD review and explicit no-default consent; non-TTY input and
.B --noconfirm
do not authorize evaluation.
The local tree is copied to an invocation-owned source snapshot and remains
unchanged. Every valid unique
.I pkgname
child declared by the accepted metadata is installed as an explicit root after
dependency planning and artifact validation.
Dependency artifacts retain dependency install reasons, and an already
explicit installed package is never demoted.
.
.TP
.B "upgrade"
Run the repository system upgrade, then strictly inspect registered
source-build preferences and rebuild configured packages when the existing
update contract requires it.
Use
.B -Syu
for the ordinary repository plus normal-AUR update when registered source
preferences must not be scanned.
.
.TP
.B "upgrade-aur"
Update installed packages that still resolve to exact AUR packages.
An exact AUR package with only a conventional devel suffix and no newer normal
AUR version is reported as requiring a check and blocks the whole AUR
execution before mutation; it is not rebuilt automatically.
For the supported reviewed single-child HTTPS Git subset, same/older package
versions use authoritative installed/reviewed provenance and a remote Git observation.
Normal version-newer precedence is unchanged. Git revision updates are not version
increases. Reviewed execution publishes actual build/install provenance; publication
failure or uncertainty after installation is a partial non-zero outcome; cleanup
failure is retained separately, without retry or a rollback claim.
Provenance schema v1 uses a separate XDG state namespace. Unknown/future schemas
and corrupt or unsafe history fail closed. Missing baselines are not generated by
the updater: they require an explicitly reviewed supported build and actual install.
A same-version reinstall that changes the installed binding invalidates historical
provenance. Dry-run performs the same read-only assessment without build or publication.
For installed AUR targets, this source-aware workflow strictly checks and
applies corresponding saved source-build preferences.
This target-less operation does not run
.B pacman -Syu
and does not update packages selected only by source-build preferences.
Its AUR-only scope means that it omits the repository system update, not that
it ignores saved preferences.
.
.TP
.B "upgrade-all"
Run the system, registered-source, fresh foreign-inventory, and filtered AUR
phases in that order.
Explicit source preferences take priority over duplicate AUR targets.
Saved source-build preferences are checked and applied strictly.
Provider selection for the filtered AUR phase completes before clone, build,
pacman, or sudo work in that phase; earlier phases may already have completed.
This is not one atomic transaction: execution stops on the first failure,
does not roll back completed package transactions, and reports later work as
not attempted.
.
.PP
Only after the repository system-upgrade phase fails, Moguet may append a
supplemental possible repository/AUR cross-source version-lock diagnostic.
It appears only when at least one candidate correlation can be presented;
otherwise the existing failure output is unchanged. The absence of
supplemental text does not itself prove candidate absence.
.
.PP
The diagnostic can show the installed package and version corresponding
to the observed repository candidate, the observed repository candidate and
version, an installed foreign package and
version with its direct exact dependency requirement, and an observed AUR
replacement candidate with its direct runtime requirement.
The foreign classification reflects that the installed package's exact name is
absent from the currently configured repository metadata; it does not prove
historical AUR provenance.
.
.PP
An observed repository candidate is read-only metadata, not the actual pacman
transaction target, and a possible candidate is not a confirmed blocker or an
identified failure cause. A compatible replacement means only that the
replacement candidate's direct runtime requirement is satisfied by the
observed repository candidate version; it does not prove pacman's selection,
the failure cause, or authorization for a safe coordinated update.
Incompatible, not-found, unknown, query-failure, and ambiguous replacement
outcomes remain distinct. A query failure is not a missing replacement, and
an incomplete or failed observation is not candidate absence.
.
.PP
This supplemental diagnostic does not replace the original pacman or sudo
output, the existing Moguet failure result, or its failure exit behavior; the
command remains failed. Moguet presents versions and dependency constraints
for manual review. It does not automatically coordinate repository/AUR
updates, remove and reinstall packages, roll back or retry the failed
transaction, create a partial upgrade, or bypass dependency checks.
.
.TP
.B "clean"
Clean the official package cache through
.B sudo pacman -Sc
and, after confirmation, the resolved Moguet cache.
The state log is not part of the reproducible cache.
.
.TP
.B "-G <pkg> [--output-dir=DIR]"
Export exactly one AUR package's complete PackageBase repository.
Without
.BR --output-dir ,
the parent is the command-start current directory.
With
.BR --output-dir=DIR ,
the parent is the named existing directory; relative values are resolved from
the command-start current directory. The validated PackageBase is always the
direct-child destination name.
The parent is not created, final and intermediate symlink components are
rejected, and Moguet does not expand a leading tilde. Use an absolute path or
an attached value such as
.BR --output-dir="$HOME/src/aur" .
An existing destination of any type is a hard failure.
Parent rename, replacement, symlink replacement, and identity drift fail
closed before the no-replace publish.
The command does not use the build cache, evaluate PKGBUILD, retrieve
dependencies, build, or install.
Only the attached output-directory form is accepted; all other global and
pacman options are unsupported for this operation.
.
.TP
.B "-Gp <pkg>"
Print only the root PKGBUILD bytes for exactly one AUR package's PackageBase
to standard output.
Diagnostics and PackageBase mapping go to standard error.
The command uses a temporary checkout and does not keep a repository, evaluate
PKGBUILD, retrieve dependencies, build, or install.
Global and pacman options are unsupported.
.
.TP
.B "deps [--recursive] <pkg>..."
Classify AUR runtime, make, and check dependencies for one or more packages.
With
.BR --recursive ,
traverse exact AUR dependencies and user-selected AUR providers.
Installed dependencies, official dependencies, uniquely resolved providers,
selected official repository providers, still-ambiguous providers, and
unresolved dependencies are displayed without further traversal. An installed
exact dependency retains Installed source identity and is not presented as an
official repository package.
On an interactive TTY, source-aware provider candidates can be selected and
the output distinguishes user-selected providers from unresolved ambiguity.
Constraint results and reasons are displayed. Unsatisfied or unknown results
warn but do not stop this read-only command; invalid or conflicting input
fails closed.
Conflict and replacement declarations are shown with their current typed
assessment, including the declaring package and any matched installed or
planned package. This read-only command does not perform replacement or
conflict resolution.
This command does not clone, build, install, or calculate a build order.
.
.TP
.B "plan <pkg>..."
Display AUR build-order plans and direct official repository package sizes for
one or more packages.
Unknown dependencies, unselected ambiguous providers, and cycles make the
plan incomplete.
The plan distinguishes uniquely resolved, user-selected, and still-ambiguous
providers.
Metadata-size unavailability does not suppress the plan body.
Unsatisfied or unknown dependency constraints make the plan incomplete and
are shown with their result and reason. Invalid or conflicting constraints
fail plan construction.
The plan also distinguishes installed conflicts, planned-target conflicts,
potential replacement impacts, unavailable or not-yet-completed judgments,
invalid metadata or observations, and a complete observation with no matching
current or planned target.
Confirmed installed or planned conflicts and potential replacement impacts can
leave plan completeness Complete while build and install require review and
remain blocked by the safety guard; Moguet does not resolve them automatically.
An unavailable or not-yet-completed relation judgment leaves completeness
Unknown and fails closed. Invalid relation metadata or observation makes
completeness Incomplete and blocks build and install.
A complete observation with no matching current or planned target adds no
relation blocker. These results do not add a separate command status taxonomy.
This command does not clone, build, or install.
.
.TP
.B "fetch <pkg>..."
Retrieve the AUR PackageBase repositories needed by complete inspection plans
for one or more packages.
A selected AUR provider's PackageBase is included; a selected official
repository provider is not cloned.
Unsatisfied or unknown dependency constraints stop before clone or fetch.
Missing repositories are cloned.
An existing clone runs only
.BR "git fetch origin" ;
Moguet does not pull, merge, reset, advance the working tree, build, or
install.
.
.TP
.B "add-src <item>..."
Register one or more source-build preferences from ordered items.
A package item starts a preference and following
.I V=K
items belong to that package until the next package item.
The v2 configuration file is not a source-preference table.
The first write creates the managed XDG directories when necessary.
.
.TP
.B "edit-src <pkg>..."
Edit one or more existing source-build preferences, or create them, using
.B VISUAL
or
.BR EDITOR .
If a failure occurs after the editor runs, Moguet retains the edited temporary
file when safe and reports its path.
.
.TP
.B "list-src"
List registered source-build preferences and their visible environment
assignments.
The complete directory snapshot is validated before any entry is printed.
.
.TP
.B "del-src <pkg>..."
Remove one or more source-build preferences without reinstalling binary
packages. A missing entry succeeds without creating preference directories.
.
.TP
.B "revert <pkg>..."
Remove one or more source-build preferences and reinstall the corresponding
official binary packages when the targets exist in configured official
repositories.
A missing preference does not create directories and does not suppress the
repository reinstall.
Repository metadata is checked before each preference is removed. A failed
observation preserves that target's preference, excludes it from reinstall,
and makes the command exit non-zero. Independent targets continue and share
the grouped reinstall; pacman failure retains diagnostic priority.
Review the displayed pacman transaction before confirming it.
.
.TP
.B "-S <pkg> | -S --select [--needed] <query>"
Install packages.
Auto routing uses official repositories first, honors an applicable source
preference, and otherwise considers AUR.
.B --aur
forces the supported target route to AUR without repository fallback;
.B --repo
forces official binary repositories without AUR or source-build fallback.
With
.BR --select ,
the single operand is a search query rather than an exact package target;
Moguet displays source-aware official-repository and AUR candidates and
requires an explicit interactive selection.
On this route,
.B --needed
applies only to each route-owned final installation.
.
.TP
.B "-Syu [--needed] | -Syu --repo [--needed]"
The exact target-less Auto form is the ordinary AUR-helper update. It performs
the official repository system upgrade first and, only after success, obtains
a fresh installed-foreign inventory and exact AUR metadata, then plans and
executes a normal installed-AUR update.
It does not snapshot, enumerate, read, or apply saved source-build preferences,
including a PackageBase fallback preference, and its preference-derived build
environment is empty.
Valid, invalid, unreadable, or failing preference data therefore does not
affect this route.
.
.PP
An independent devel target whose status is
.B RequiresCheck
is skipped with a non-blocking warning and does not stop unrelated normal AUR
updates. This state remains unverified: it is neither UpToDate nor an automatic
update decision. If another update candidate requires the target through a
dependency, provider, or required-child relation, the affected root is blocked
and the command remains non-zero. The explicit
.B upgrade-aur
and
.B upgrade-all
routes retain their strict whole-operation RequiresCheck blocker behavior.
.
.PP
The phases are sequential, not atomic. A repository failure leaves the AUR
phase not attempted and exits non-zero. If the repository phase completes but
the AUR phase is blocked or fails, Moguet reports repository completion and a
non-zero partial failure without rollback. Cleanup failure remains distinct
from installation outcome, an inconsistent aggregate fails closed, and an AUR
NoUpdates result alone does not make the whole operation NoOp.
.
.PP
For Auto, the only initially supported pacman semantic option is
.BR --needed ;
it is kept only in the exact ordered repository transaction and is not applied
to the later AUR transaction. Any other pacman semantic option or unsupported
argument form is rejected before repository mutation, with guidance to use
.BR "moguet -Syu --repo" .
The RepoOnly form removes the semantic selector before invoking pacman,
preserves the compatible pacman pass-through tail, performs only the
repository system upgrade, and does not query AUR, read source preferences, or
invoke cache, Git, makepkg, or source-runner work.
.B -Syu --aur
is unsupported; use source-aware
.B upgrade-aur
for an AUR-only update.
.
.PP
Only the exact canonical target-less token has this combined meaning.
.BR -Sy ,
.BR -Su ,
.BR -Suy ,
separated or long modifier spellings, target-bearing
.BR "-Syu <pkg>" ,
and unknown modifier forms retain their existing routing and do not start an
installed-AUR sweep.
.
.TP
.B "-Ss <query>"
Search packages.
Auto mode combines official repository and AUR results.
Installed annotations use only a successful foreign-package inventory.
An unavailable inventory produces a warning and omits annotations without
changing the search match/exit policy. AUR-only search skips this metadata query.
.B --aur
uses only AUR and does not refresh pacman databases;
.B --repo
uses only official repositories.
.
.TP
.B "-Si <pkg>"
Show package information.
Auto mode prefers official repository information and falls back to exact AUR
metadata only when the package is authoritatively absent. Metadata failure
is reported without AUR fallback; the failed operand is excluded from pacman
while independent targets continue, and the command exits non-zero.
AUR info retains installed yes/no on successful observation. Unavailable
installed state is shown with a warning instead of no; this optional annotation
failure alone does not change the info exit policy.
Source selectors restrict the lookup to their named source.
For AUR metadata, declared conflicts and replacements are shown as metadata;
the installed/planned assessment is explicitly deferred to planning and build
preflight.
.
.TP
.B "-Qua"
Ask pacman for foreign-package updates, including installed packages that may
have AUR updates.
Conventional exact-AUR devel suffix candidates without a newer normal version
are shown with a check-required reason instead of a version-update arrow.
This check-required result alone retains query exit status zero.
This remains a pacman-compatible query and is distinct from executing
.BR upgrade-aur .
Except for the two exact target-less
.B -Syu
semantic forms documented above, the pacman-compatible forms are examples of
delegated open grammar, not a closed allowlist. The repository-only
.B -Syu --repo
form also keeps a compatible delegated pacman tail. Arguments that Moguet does
not consume remain owned by pacman when the selected route can preserve their
meaning.
.\" PUBLIC COMMANDS END
.
.\" parity:options
.SH OPTIONS
.\" PUBLIC OPTIONS BEGIN
.TP
.B "-h, --help"
Show localized help and exit without creating XDG directories.
.
.TP
.B "-V, --version"
Show
.B Moguet
and the program version, then exit without creating XDG directories.
.
.TP
.B "--dry-run"
Observe a supported Moguet-owned mutating route by using its production
pre-mutation authorities and the unified human-readable plan renderer.
The supported routes are Moguet-owned
.B -S
install and system-update forms such as
.BR -Syu ,
.BR fetch ,
remote and local
.BR build ,
.BR upgrade ,
.BR upgrade-aur ,
and
.BR upgrade-all .
Scope-excluded
.BR deps ,
.BR plan ,
.BR -Ss ,
.BR -Si ,
.BR clean ,
and generic pacman pass-through forms are rejected explicitly.
.
.PP
Read-only filesystem, network, and exact allowlisted pacman discovery queries
may run, but dry-run does not write the state log or persistent state, create a
cache, workspace, or worktree, run Git clone/fetch/checkout mutation, evaluate
local metadata with
.BR "makepkg --printsrcinfo" ,
produce build output, invoke sudo, start or mutate through a pacman
transaction, acquire a pacman transaction lock, install packages, or perform
cleanup mutation.
The local route uses only an already safe descriptor; if metadata evaluation
would be required, the observation is
.B Blocked
instead of guessed ready.
.
.PP
.B Ready
and
.B NoOp
observations exit zero;
.B Blocked
exits non-zero.
The observation is not an approval token, prepared execution capability, or
cached provider choice. A later actual invocation revalidates current state.
Moguet v2.2.0 provides this human-readable surface only; no JSON or other
machine-readable plan schema is introduced.
.
.PP
For exact target-less
.BR "--dry-run -Syu" ,
the repository system-update intent and later normal-AUR transaction intents
are displayed separately. The AUR assessment is based on the current installed
state and is not a prediction of the post-repository state. Actual execution
does not reuse the observation or a prepared capability; after repository
success it obtains a fresh installed-foreign inventory, AUR metadata, plan,
provider decisions, and preflight. A current-state AUR NoUpdates result does
not turn the outer repository-bearing operation into NoOp.
.BR "--dry-run -Syu --repo"
displays only the repository intent and does not query AUR or source-build
preferences.
.
.TP
.B "--edit"
Select the prompt policy for opening or editing PKGBUILD and detected top-level
.I *.install
files for this invocation.
This overrides
.BR review.pkgbuild .
It is invocation-local editor policy, not upstream reviewed-source acceptance,
and cannot advance a reviewed revision.
.
.TP
.B "--noedit"
Skip invocation-local PKGBUILD and detected top-level
.I *.install
editing for this invocation.
It neither accepts nor skips the separate upstream reviewed-source decision.
It does not disable source, artifact, identity, or transaction validation.
.
.TP
.B "--diff"
Select the prompt policy for reviewing AUR source changes from the previous
reviewed revision to the exact fetched target. If there is no reviewed state,
or the old baseline object is unavailable, the safe review is a full current
tracked-file review rather than a cache-HEAD fallback.
This overrides
.BR review.diff .
Only explicit acceptance after a complete review advances reviewed state.
.
.TP
.B "--nodiff"
Skip the reviewed-source change review and acceptance path for this invocation.
It does not advance reviewed state. Unsafe, future, or inconsistent state is
still fail-closed rather than treated as missing or bypassed.
It does not authorize discarding user modifications or destructive Git
operations.
.
.TP
.B "--noconfirm"
Pass non-confirmation behavior to supported pacman and makepkg execution and
avoid Moguet prompts by using their defined defaults.
Provider selection has no default: this option does not read stdin, prompt, or
select a provider, and unresolved ambiguity fails closed.
Root package discovery also stops before its candidate query and never chooses
a package automatically.
Local PKGBUILD metadata evaluation likewise has no default; this option never
authorizes
.BR "makepkg --printsrcinfo" .
This is not \(dqyes to everything\(dq and does not bypass unresolved or
ambiguous dependencies, cycles, source selection, conflicts/replacements,
artifact identity, ownership, or other safety guards.
.
.TP
.B "--output-dir=DIR"
Select an existing export parent for
.BR -G .
This operation-local option requires a non-empty attached value, may appear
only once, is not stored in configuration, and is not supported by
.BR -Gp
or any other operation. Relative values use the command-start current
directory. Moguet does not create the parent, follow symlink components, or
perform tilde expansion.
.
.TP
.B "--select"
With plain
.BR -S ,
treat exactly one operand as a source-aware package search query and require an
explicit selection before installation. Auto mode searches official
repositories and AUR;
.B --aur
or
.B --repo
limits the candidate source. Number, multiple-number, inclusive-range, and
displayed-official-group selectors are supported on an interactive TTY. Only
.B --needed
is a shared pacman option for both selected routes.
.
.TP
.B "--needed"
Treat this as a pacman-compatible option.
Pacman-only routes keep it in the ordered argument list.
For Auto combined
.BR -Syu ,
it is the only initially supported pacman semantic option and is kept only in
the repository transaction, not the later normal-AUR transaction. RepoOnly
.B -Syu --repo
keeps it in the repository pass-through.
On supported AUR or source-build
.B -S
routes, apply it only once to final
.B pacman -U
installation.
It does not skip planning, clone/fetch, review, validation, or build.
.
.TP
.B "--build-mode=normal|rebuild|clean"
Select the source-build mode for this invocation.
The built-in default is
.BR normal .
The
.B rebuild
mode permits rebuilding an existing artifact; the
.B clean
mode also requests a clean source build.
.
.TP
.B "--rebuild"
Compatibility alias for
.BR --build-mode=rebuild .
.
.TP
.B "--cleanbuild"
Compatibility alias for
.BR --build-mode=clean .
.
.TP
.B "--rmdeps"
Recognize the legacy cleanup request but reject it on separated source-build
routes before mutation.
Moguet cannot prove the exact dependency set owned by the invocation and does
not translate this option to
.BR "makepkg -r" ,
.BR "pacman -Rns" ,
or custom orphan cleanup.
.
.TP
.B "--aur"
Limit supported
.BR -S ,
.BR -Ss ,
and
.B -Si
forms to AUR, without official repository fallback.
It is not supported for
.BR -Syu ,
target-less upgrades, or Moguet-specific inspection commands. Use
.B upgrade-aur
for the source-aware AUR-only update; AUR-only means no repository system
update and does not mean that saved source preferences are ignored.
.
.TP
.B "--repo"
Limit supported
.BR -S ,
.BR -Ss ,
and
.B -Si
forms to official binary repositories, without AUR or source-build fallback.
With exact target-less
.BR -Syu ,
select the repository-only system upgrade. The selector is not passed to
pacman, and compatible remaining pacman arguments are preserved. This form
does not inventory or query AUR and does not invoke source preferences, cache,
Git, makepkg, or the source runner.
It does not delete an existing source preference.
.\" PUBLIC OPTIONS END
.
.PP
Repeating the same source selector is allowed.
Combining
.B --aur
and
.B --repo
fails before an external command or AUR query.
Conflicting review, diff, or build-mode overrides fail before mutation rather
than using last-one-wins behavior.
.
.\" parity:configuration
.SH CONFIGURATION
Moguet reads one optional, user-owned TOML file:
.
.nf
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/moguet/config.toml
fallback: ~/.config/moguet/config.toml
.fi
.
.PP
The v2.0.0 schema and built-in defaults are:
.
.nf
schema_version = 1

[review]
pkgbuild = "prompt"
diff = "prompt"

[build]
mode = "normal"
.fi
.
.PP
Values are composed in this order:
.
.nf
built-in defaults -> user config -> CLI override
.fi
.
.PP
.B review.diff
and
.BR --diff / --nodiff
select the AUR reviewed-source prompt policy. Skipping it never advances
reviewed state.
.B review.pkgbuild
and
.BR --edit / --noedit
select invocation-local PKGBUILD and
.I *.install
editor behavior; they are not upstream review acceptance.
.
.PP
A missing file is normal.
An existing file requires integer
.B schema_version = 1
and is validated strictly.
Invalid TOML, unknown keys, type errors, invalid enum values, and unsupported
future schema versions stop before external mutation.
Moguet treats the file as read-only input and does not create, rewrite, or
migrate it automatically.
It does not create or read
.I /etc/moguet
as a system-wide configuration layer.
.
.\" parity:files
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/moguet/config.toml
Optional user configuration.
The fallback is
.IR ~/.config/moguet/config.toml .
.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/moguet/source-build.d/<package-name>
User-owned per-package source-build preference.
The fallback is
.IR $HOME/.config/moguet/source-build.d/<package-name> .
The managed directories use mode 0700 and preference entries use mode 0600.
All source-preference commands, source-aware builds, and explicit
.B upgrade*
readers use this authority strictly. Exact target-less
.B -Syu
and its dry-run deliberately do not snapshot or read the directory, try a
PackageBase fallback preference, or apply a preference-derived environment.
.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moguet/moguet.log
Default human-readable log.
The fallback is
.IR ~/.local/state/moguet/moguet.log .
.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moguet/reviewed-sources/aur/
Persistent PackageBase-scoped reviewed AUR revision state.
The fallback is
.IR ~/.local/state/moguet/reviewed-sources/aur/ .
It is separate from reproducible cache and survives cache deletion or
recloning. Read-only lookup does not create the store.
.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/moguet/
Reproducible repository and build cache.
The fallback is
.IR ~/.cache/moguet/ .
Cache is not authoritative state.
.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/moguet.1
English authority man page.
.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/ja/man1/moguet.1
Formal Japanese translation of this man page.
.
.TP
.I /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/moguet
Bash completion for the public CLI schema.
.
.TP
.I /usr/share/zsh/site-functions/_moguet
zsh completion for the public CLI schema.
.
.TP
.I /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/moguet.fish
fish completion for the public CLI schema.
.
.TP
.I /usr/share/locale/ja/LC_MESSAGES/moguet.mo
Japanese GNU gettext runtime catalog.
.
.\" parity:environment
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute base directory for user configuration.
An unset or empty value falls back to
.IR $HOME/.config .
For source-preference access, an explicit value must be absolute, must already
exist, and must pass the ownership, type, and permission checks.
Moguet creates only the source-preference managed children below that base when
a write operation first needs them.
.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Absolute base directory for persistent runtime state and the default log.
An unset or empty value falls back to
.IR $HOME/.local/state .
.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Absolute base directory for reproducible cache.
An unset or empty value falls back to
.IR $HOME/.cache .
.
.TP
.B HOME
Used only for standard XDG fallbacks when the corresponding XDG variable is
unset or empty.
An unusable home or unsafe path fails closed.
The source-preference write boundary may create the required fallback config
hierarchy; read-only operations do not.
.
.TP
.B VISUAL
Preferred editor.
Resolution order is
.B VISUAL
then
.B EDITOR
then
.BR nano .
.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Second editor choice when
.B VISUAL
is unset or empty.
.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL , " LC_MESSAGES" , " LANG" , " LANGUAGE"
Standard process-locale inputs used by GNU gettext.
English is the source authority and fallback; Japanese is a formally supported
translation.
There is no
.B --lang
option or TOML language key.
.
.\" parity:safety
.SH SAFETY
Moguet stops before the relevant external mutation when it cannot determine
dependency, provider, PackageBase, source, artifact, ownership, or transaction
state authoritatively.
It does not use
.B --noconfirm
to cross such a guard.
.
.SS "INTERACTIVE CONFIRMATION"
Moguet-owned boolean prompts use
.B [Y/n]
for a Yes default,
.B [y/N]
for a No default, and
.B [y/n]
when there is no default.
The fixed, locale-neutral, case-insensitive ASCII responses are
.BR y / yes ,
.BR n / no ,
and
.BR q / quit / cancel .
The q-family cancels the current Moguet operation instead of acting as a
question-specific No. Other input warns and re-prompts. Empty input at
.B [y/n]
also warns and re-prompts; it is never implicit approval.
.
.PP
.B --noconfirm
uses only a declared default: Yes for
.B [Y/n]
and the safe No for
.BR [y/N] .
It cannot answer
.BR [y/n] .
Non-TTY standard input may use only the safe
.B [y/N]
No default; it does not select the Yes default or approve a no-default prompt.
.
.PP
Clean EOF during an interactive confirmation cancels with an end-of-input
reason. An actual stream read failure remains an input failure. Neither is
treated as implicit Yes.
.
.PP
A decline is the negative answer owned by the question; cancellation stops the
current Moguet operation. Both are presented separately from actual input,
external-command, build, validation, or internal failures. Presentation
severity and process status are independent: an optional No or normal skip may
complete with status zero, while a decline, cancellation, EOF, or unavailable
approval that leaves a required operation incomplete is non-zero.
An input failure and other actual failures are also non-zero.
.
.PP
Cancellation stops work from that point onward. It does not imply that the
whole invocation was side-effect free and does not roll back an already
completed Git, editor, pacman, or earlier system phase.
.
.PP
For AUR Git source builds, Moguet stores the last explicitly accepted exact
upstream commit for each PackageBase. Missing state starts an initial full
tracked-file review. A different target is reviewed from the previous reviewed
revision, the same target needs no prompt or rewrite, and an unavailable old
commit requires a full rebaseline review instead of a cache-HEAD fallback.
Invalid, corrupted, or source-mismatched current state requires an explicit
full rebind review. Future schema and unsafe or inconsistent history fail
closed without overwrite.
.
.PP
The review inventory retains every tracked added, modified, deleted, renamed,
or type-changed file. Root PKGBUILD and top-level
.I *.install
files receive review-sensitive guidance, but patches, service units, helper
scripts, local source/config files, binary changes, and other tracked content
are not filtered out.
.I .SRCINFO
is lower-priority generated metadata, not source-review authority.
.
.PP
Displaying a review is not acceptance. Only an explicit interactive
.B y
or
.B yes
after a complete review can advance state. A
.BR --nodiff
skip, review decline,
.BR --noconfirm ,
or non-TTY input may keep a compatibility-only build route but does not advance
state. Cancellation, EOF, input failure, unsupported review, and unsafe or
future state stop without advancement.
.
.PP
An accepted AUR build uses the exact target OID in a detached checkout;
mutable HEAD, branches, and remote refs are not build authority. State
publication uses compare-and-swap semantics and does not overwrite another
process's reviewed result. A later build or install failure does not roll back
a correctly accepted and published revision.
.BR --edit / --noedit
controls an invocation-local editor overlay that is separate from the upstream
reviewed revision. Official-repository and local PKGBUILD routes do not create
reviewed-source state.
.
.PP
Before build or install, Moguet assesses declared conflicts and replacements
against installed and planned packages, including provided components and
versioned relations. Diagnostics distinguish installed conflicts from planned
target conflicts. A matching replacement is only a potential impact requiring
review; Moguet does not remove, replace, or resolve packages automatically.
Unavailable or invalid judgments fail closed and are not reported as absence.
Only a complete observation with no matching current or planned package or
provided component releases that relation guard. The declaration remains, and
pacman/libalpm remains the transaction authority.
.
.PP
When multiple dependency providers remain, an interactive TTY displays
source-aware numbered candidates and requires exactly one selection, with no
default. Empty input, q, quit, cancel, or EOF cancels; invalid or out-of-range
input retries. Non-TTY use and
.B --noconfirm
do not read provider input from stdin and fail closed. A choice is shared only
within the current invocation. Selected AUR PackageBases flow into fetch and
build planning; a selected official provider is introduced as an exact
.I repository/package
dependency.
.
.PP
When the interactive provider list is actually displayed, Moguet looks up each
candidate package name in the read-only local package database. It appends the
localized tag
.B [installed]
only for a same-name local package, leaves an authoritative absence untagged,
and displays
.B [installed state unknown]
with a separate warning when the lookup is unavailable. This name-only
observation does not prove source provenance, PackageBase, version or
constraint compatibility, or install reason; it does not change candidate
order, numbering, choice reuse, routing, or the required explicit choice.
.
.PP
Root package discovery through
.B -S --select
also has no default, even for one candidate. An interactive TTY accepts one or
more package numbers, inclusive ranges, and an
.B @group
selector for a displayed official group. Empty input, q, quit, cancel, or EOF
cancels; invalid input retries against the same candidate snapshot. Non-TTY
stdin and
.B --noconfirm
stop before candidate queries or prompts. After every selected root completes
static preflight, exact
.I repository/package
targets run first in one repository transaction; only its success allows the
selected AUR roots to enter the existing source-build lifecycle. A later AUR
failure does not roll back the completed repository transaction.
.
.PP
The registered AUR route offers provider selection only when every candidate
is from an official repository. A candidate set containing an AUR provider
remains ambiguous and fails closed before system or source execution, because
this singular compatibility route cannot schedule that provider's PackageBase.
.
.PP
Official-repository source identity comes from the exact configured libalpm
snapshot. Only a confirmed
.B NotFound
may fall back to AUR; query, configuration, or metadata failure stops instead
of being treated as absence. Standalone official builds use
.BR PackageBaseSet ;
registered official sources use it after
.B OnlyIfUpdated
preparation. They build the authoritative PackageBase once, install only the
requested explicit child, and report sibling and debug outputs as unselected
and not installed. The sync repository route remains
.B SingularCompatibility
with its existing
.B --needed
behavior, and registered AUR remains
.B SingularCompatibility
with its existing provider and split-package guards.
.
.PP
.B deps
and
.B plan
do not clone, build, or install.
.B fetch
does not update an existing working tree.
The export commands do not build or install.
External commands and privilege escalation remain visible to the user.
.
.PP
A local PKGBUILD build uses an invocation-owned source snapshot and never
resets, cleans, overwrites, or deletes the user-owned source tree. It does not
require Git and does not query AUR for the local root. Unsafe source or metadata
state, an unapproved metadata evaluation, an incomplete dependency plan, or an
unproven artifact stops before the corresponding mutation.
.
.PP
Source-build PackageBase work uses a fresh artifact destination, validates all
expected outputs, selects only required child package identities, and hands
validated artifacts to one pacman transaction per PackageBase.
Unknown, missing, duplicate, unexpected, or unrepresentable identities fail
closed.
.
.PP
Multi-phase updates are not atomic.
A failure does not automatically roll back already completed package
transactions.
A cleanup failure after successful installation is partial success and must not
be retried blindly.
For exact target-less
.BR -Syu ,
the repository system transaction completes before any fresh AUR authority is
obtained. Repository failure leaves the AUR phase not attempted; a later AUR
blocker or failure is non-zero partial completion and does not roll back the
repository transaction.
.
.\" parity:examples
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Perform the ordinary repository plus normal installed-AUR update:
.RS
.B moguet -Syu
.RE
.
.TP
Perform only the repository system upgrade:
.RS
.B moguet -Syu --repo
.RE
.
.TP
Discover and explicitly select source-aware install targets:
.RS
.B moguet -S --select fastfetch
.RE
.
.TP
Build and install all declared package children from a local PKGBUILD root:
.RS
.B moguet build --local .
.RE
.
.TP
Install an AUR package without repository fallback:
.RS
.B moguet -S --aur google-chrome
.RE
.
.TP
Install an official binary while ignoring a source preference for this run:
.RS
.B moguet -S --repo fastfetch
.RE
.
.TP
Inspect an AUR dependency graph without cloning or building:
.RS
.B moguet deps --recursive google-chrome
.RE
.
.TP
Export a PackageBase under an existing relative parent:
.RS
.B moguet -G wezterm-git --output-dir=./exports
.RE
.
.TP
View a build plan without mutation:
.RS
.B moguet plan mongodb-bin
.RE
.
.TP
Update all supported scopes in the documented phase order:
.RS
.B moguet upgrade-all
.RE
.
.TP
Temporarily restore review and normal build defaults over user config:
.RS
.B moguet --edit --diff --build-mode=normal -S google-chrome
.RE
.
.\" parity:migration
.SH MIGRATION
Starting with Moguet v2.6.0, exact target-less
.B moguet -Syu
changes from repository-only behavior to the ordinary AUR-helper update:
repository system update followed by a normal installed-AUR update, without
reading or applying saved source-build preferences. Existing users who need
the former repository-only behavior must use
.BR "moguet -Syu --repo" .
Use
.BR "moguet upgrade" ,
.BR "moguet upgrade-aur" ,
or
.B "moguet upgrade-all"
when saved source-build preferences must be checked and applied. The combined
route is sequential and non-atomic; a later AUR failure reports partial
completion and does not roll back the completed repository transaction.
.
.PP
An existing Moguet AUR cache from before reviewed-source state requires no
manual migration. No record is a normal missing state and causes one initial
full review for the first affected PackageBase. Moguet does not invent a
reviewed revision from legacy checkout HEAD, a branch, a remote ref, or build
artifacts. Invalid, corrupted, source-mismatched, future, unsafe, or
inconsistent state is not treated as missing.
.
.PP
Starting with Moguet v2.0.1, Moguet does not read
.I /etc/jpacker/jpacker.conf
as a normal configuration layer or
.I /etc/jpacker/package.build/
as a source-preference fallback.  It does not automatically copy, merge,
rewrite, or delete
.IR /etc/jpacker .
Root-owned legacy data is not assigned to a user by inference.
Legacy entries are ignored by Moguet and remain available for manual migration
and rollback.
.
.PP
Back up jpacker v1.16.0 data, install the validated Moguet package alongside it,
and map only understood settings by hand.  The packages have disjoint payloads
and no provides, conflicts, or replaces relationship.  Moguet supplies no
.B jpacker
command alias.  Keep the v1 package during verification for a direct rollback,
or remove it explicitly only after the Moguet checks pass.  Do not run mutating
package operations from both helpers concurrently, although their
source-preference stores are not shared.  Recreate only understood legacy
entries, one package and one explicitly selected target user at a time; do not
overwrite an existing XDG entry or delete the legacy entry.  Run Moguet as that
normal user, not through sudo.  Source-preference filesystem operations do not
use sudo; a revert may still use sudo for its pacman package transaction.
.B NOEDIT
maps to
.BR review.pkgbuild ;
.B NODIFF
maps to
.BR review.diff ;
legacy
.BR EDITOR ,
.BR LOGFILE ,
and
.B RMDEPS
are not copied into TOML.
Consult
.I docs/migration/v1-to-v2.md
or
.I /usr/share/doc/moguet/docs/migration/v1-to-v2.md
for backup, completion/man verification, optional v1 removal, and rollback
instructions.
.
.\" parity:see-also
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR makepkg (8),
.BR git (1)
.
